@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ What Callisto promises to keep working from 1.0, and what it does not. A breakin
 | --- | --- |
 | The eight commands (`add`, `status`, `version`, `pre`, `snapshot`, `init`, `release`, `completions`) and their flags | A flag keeps its meaning; a new flag never changes what the command did without it. |
 | `--dry-run` | Accepted by every command, before or after the command name. Commands that write write nothing under it; on read-only commands it does nothing; where it cannot apply (for example `release plan`) it is a usage error. |
-| Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error: a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing; the same value read from `callisto.toml`, a changeset or another file is a failure, not a usage error. |
+| Exit codes | `0` success, `1` failure, `2` usage error: a bad or missing argument or flag, including values the command validates after parsing; the same value read from `callisto.toml`, a changeset or another file is a failure, not a usage error. `130` is a cancelled prompt: Esc or Ctrl-C at an interactive question (`add`, `init`) ended the command, and nothing was written. |
 | `--format json` reports | Every report carries `schemaVersion`. Within a version a field is not removed, renamed or retyped; fields may be added. A shape change bumps the version. `release inspect` prints the intent, manifest or receipt unchanged: its own `schemaVersion`, no `command` or `dryRun`. `schema` prints JSON Schema documents, not reports. With `--format json` a failed command writes nothing to stdout and ends stderr with one JSON error document (`schemaVersion`, `command`, `dryRun`, `error` with `code`, `message`, `help`, `path`) and exits `1`; output from a tool the command ran may precede it. Argument-parsing errors (an unknown flag or a missing value) are the exception: they print clap's usage text and exit `2`. |
 | `callisto.toml` | A key keeps its meaning. Unknown keys are an error, so a new key arrives in a minor release and never changes an existing file's behavior. |
 | Changesets | The `.changeset/*.md` format and `pre.json` stay compatible with `@changesets/cli` 2.x and 3.x. `pre.json` is read in either shape and written back in the shape read: 2.x (`mode`, `tag`, `initialVersions`, `changesets`) or 3.x (`mode`, `tag`, with applied notes in `.changeset/pre/`). A cycle `callisto pre enter` starts uses the 2.x shape. The bare package name is the key unless another ecosystem has a package of that name, in which case the key is `ecosystem/name`. |
  95 }
